{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '92,123p' perception.py\ncat legs_log.md\"","aggregated_output":"def object_candidates(frame, cell: int = 4, min_area: int = 4) -> List[dict]:\n    \"\"\"A compact, game-agnostic object list from color components and cell signatures.\"\"\"\n    f = arr(frame)\n    blobs = connected_components(f, min_area=min_area)\n    sigs = block_signatures(f, cell)\n    objects = []\n    for b in blobs:\n        r0, c0, r1, c1 = b.bbox\n        objects.append({\n            \"color\": b.color,\n            \"bbox\": b.bbox,\n            \"top_left\": b.top_left,\n            \"size\": b.size,\n            \"area\": b.area,\n            \"centroid\": b.centroid,\n            \"cell\": (r0 // cell, c0 // cell),\n            \"cell_sig\": sigs.get((r0 // cell, c0 // cell)),\n        })\n    return objects\n\n\ndef frame_delta(before, after) -> dict:\n    a, b = arr(before), arr(after)\n    ys, xs = np.where(a != b)\n    if len(ys) == 0:\n        return {\"count\": 0, \"bbox\": None, \"samples\": []}\n    samples = [(int(y), int(x), int(a[y, x]), int(b[y, x])) for y, x in zip(ys[:80], xs[:80])]\n    return {\n        \"count\": int(len(ys)),\n        \"bbox\": (int(ys.min()), int(xs.min()), int(ys.max()), int(xs.max())),\n        \"samples\": samples,\n    }\n# Leg-library debrief log\n\nRecurring composition patterns and repeated novelty.\n\n## Level 1: switchable platforms (verified)\n- Public clone probes identify color 14 as the avatar: keys 1/2/3/4 move it by two pixels up/down/left/right on connected colored platforms. From pristine entry, repeated up stops at (row 38, col 10) until the lower bridge moves.\n- Coordinate button (48,36) alternates the color 9 bridge between bbox (20,18,23,21) and (34,8,37,11). Button (48,20) alternates color 8 between bbox (30,12,33,17) and (24,18,29,21). Both effects were reproduced from entry and with the avatar at different pad positions.\n- Verified subgoals: lower bridge -> red platform at (30,10) -> purple platform at (30,20) -> upper bridge at (24,20) -> destination color 11 at (20,24). The lower button must be toggled back after crossing it to restore the final connection.\n- Dense progress: Manhattan distance from avatar to destination divided by the observed two-pixel stride. Clone A* retains the visible bridge state and omits the observed bottom-row move meter.\n- candidate_switch_walkways.json contains an independently clone-verified 20-action route. The reusable search also passed the real harness: RESULT levels=1 moves=20 replay_ok=True err=None.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > probe_level3.py <<'PY'\nimport json, time\nimport gkm_try as H\nfrom perception import arr, object_candidates, action_deltas, safe_step, connected_components\n\ndef entry(env):\n    with open('checkpoint.json') as f: path=json.load(f)['final_path']\n    for a in path: safe_step(env,a)\n\ndef describe(env):\n    return [(b.color,b.bbox,b.area) for b in connected_components(env.frame())]\n\ndef probe(env):\n    entry(env)\n    print('ENTRY',env.levels_completed,'actions',env.actions)\n    print('OBJECTS',describe(env))\n    print('KEYS',action_deltas(env))\n    f=arr(env.frame())\n    print('GRID2')\n    for r in range(0,62,2):\n        print(f'{r:02}', ''.join(format(int(f[r,c]),'x') for c in range(0,64,2)))\n    return\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    print(H.A.run_program('dc22',probe)[:1])\nPY\npython probe_level3.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
